# Drafts Layer Conventions

`drafts/` and any `*.draft.mdx` file are listed in `.mintignore`. Nothing here
is built, validated, or searchable. Use it for a page that is not ready for
navigation. Article maps live in
`.agents/skills/guides-architecture/maps/`, not here.

## Structure

```text
drafts/<anything>.mdx           # draft pages awaiting review
<tab>/<page>.draft.mdx          # draft next to its final location
```

## Patterns

- A draft page keeps its final frontmatter so promoting it is a rename plus
  a navigation entry.
- Promote by moving the file out of `drafts/` (or dropping `.draft`), adding
  it to `config/navigation/index.json`, and running `npm run validate`.

## Boundaries

- Nothing in `drafts/` is linked from a published page; `mint broken-links`
  does not see it.
- No secrets or customer data, even though it is unpublished; the repo is
  shared.
- Do not let a draft outlive its usefulness. Delete a draft once it is promoted.
